{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to `d7f7ce23`: the LS-5 diagnostic ran on Linux.\n\nHead `aef057a9f1bee29b52806be8c36244f4cc68bad9`, branch\n`diag/ls5-20261115`, Local Worker smoke run 43785373777, failure in\nabout 40 s. The one diagnostic line, complete:\n\n- `stage: smoke`, `signal: null`, `operation: install`,\n  `detail: transport-no-answer`.\n- `transport`: `kind: reply-not-answer`, `status: 4xx`,\n  `statusCode: 410`.\n- `exchange`: `clientPhase: response-complete`,\n  `firstFailure: none`, `errorClass: none`,\n  `proxyDecision: forwarded`, `upstreamPhase: response-complete`,\n  `upstreamEnd: complete`, `downstreamEnd: finished`,\n  `clientBodyEnd: complete`, `clientStop: none`,\n  `upstreamStatus: 4xx`, `clientStatus: 4xx`,\n  `startupHealth: http-503`, `startupSessions: ok`,\n  `proxy: listening`, `worker: running`,\n  `upstreamStatusCode: 410`, `clientStatusCode: 410`,\n  `replyBodyClass: json-object-other`,\n  `faultBoundary: backend-reply`, `owner: celldbackend`.\n\nThe owner differs from run 43781291767, which named the proxy. Say\nwhich classification is right and why the first one named the proxy.\n\nMy reading, for you to check from source: the Worker answers 410 in\ntwo places. `roomRetiredResponse` in\n`packages/scope/src/room-retired.ts` sends a JSON object with three\nmembers, which fits `json-object-other` and is no answer. The\n`archived` answer at `packages/scope/src/worker.ts:428` is an\nanswer, so it does not fit. If the first holds, the Worker under\ncelld judges the newly planned register as a retired room.\n\nNext: name the branch of the source that sends this 410 for a new\ninstall, and why it holds on Linux under celld and not in the local\ngate. One more diagnostic run is available at once if you need a\nclosed class for the `error` member. Then the fix goes by the\nordinary route.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}